concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-consequential-and-transitional-provisions-act-2001-sch-2-sec-9 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9 After subsection 56(5)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-9 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (5A) It is not an offence if the production by a person of a document that was given to APRA under section 9 or 13 of the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001 is to the Australian Statistician for the purposes of the Census and Statistics Act 1905. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to matters in subsection (5A) (see section 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (5B) It is not an offence if the production by a person of a document that was given to APRA under section 9 or 13 of the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001 is to:  (a) the Reserve Bank of Australia; or  (b) another prescribed authority. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to matters in subsection (5B) (see section 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (5C) If a document relating to a financial sector entity (other than an entity that is, or is included in a class of entities that are, excluded by the regulations from the operation of this subsection) is a reporting document that:  (a) was given by the entity to APRA under section 13 of the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001; and  Schedule 2  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (5A) It is not an offence if the production by a person of a document that was given to APRA under section 9 or 13 of the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001 is to the Australian Statistician for the purposes of the Census and Statistics Act 1905. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to matters in subsection (5A) (see section 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (5B) It is not an offence if the production by a person of a document that was given to APRA under section 9 or 13 of the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001 is to:  (a) the Reserve Bank of Australia; or  (b) another prescribed authority. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to matters in subsection (5B) (see section 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (5C) If a document relating to a financial sector entity (other than an entity that is, or is included in a class of entities that are, excluded by the regulations from the operation of this subsection) is a reporting document that:  (a) was given by the entity to APRA under section 13 of the Financial Sector (Collection of Data) Act 2001; and  Schedule 2  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-consequential-and-transitional-provisions-act-2001-sch-2-sec-9-ss-5a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-consequential-and-transitional-provisions-act-2001-sch-2-sec-9-ss-5b ;
    cml:hasPart concept:financial-sector-collection-of-data-consequential-and-transitional-provisions-act-2001-sch-2-sec-9-ss-5c ;
